00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.900
Corrections: None.{"Default" from "Top" -A0}

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.050
Permission to fire: Granted.{"Default" from "Top" -A0}

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.130
Good work.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.050
All of the targets on the runway have been eliminated.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.230
Over and out.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.300
What're you doing?

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:20.020
These things are numb. I've been laying down here since this morning.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.830
If you don't mind, I could massage them.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.040
I would if you were a better shot than me.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.030
But you're one of the top five officers in our whole country.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:34.950
That's no fair.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.070
You'd better give up then.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:38.880
Anyway...

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.300
How did those things even get here? We're on a floating airport that can only be reached by ship.{"at a seaside" to "on a floating" for clarity -A0}

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.790
Haven't they been restricting entry?

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.370
Yeah.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:52.220
Only high ranking officials and airport technicians as well as their families are allowed in.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.850
One of them must've been infected.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.360
The situation is under control right now, but who knows how long that'll last?

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.230
What do you think would've happened to this place

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.200
if we hadn't been assigned here due to terrorist threats?

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.850
Well, I don't have infinite ammo...

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.050
You're gonna run away?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.020
Not planning on it.

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.080
Well, not yet.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.750
I'm gonna go to the city.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.080
Eventually.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.160
What, you have a guy there?

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:35.490
Nah, a friend.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.420
That's right.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.630
Thus, instead of acting out of self-interest,

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:46.080
we need to find a safe place and move as a group.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.570
For example, we shouldn't all go check on our families

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.690
until we become an organized group.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.360
In fact, I think the number one thing for us right now

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.470
Hirano.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.540
is laying down a foundation for our group.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:02.780
Understand?

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:03.050
Takagi-san...

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.590
Good morning, sunshine.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.300
Why did you fall asleep?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.630
And you're drooling!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.180
Because of... all this.{include koreja}

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:20.730
I think it would've been better if we had gone toward the suburbs.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:24.090
There are other ways to escape besides cars.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.650
The floating airport?{"seaside" to "floating" for consistancy -A0}

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.390
As you can see, it's too dangerous to be in the city.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.720
There's probably a group of people who are trying to flee to an island

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.900
or to some isolated area where there are armed forces.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.790
Like Okinawa?

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:44.830
The American military forces that're stationed there aren't there to fight.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.980
Oh, but there is the SDF...

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:52.940
Hokkaido and Kyushu should be okay if they handled the situation appropriately.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:57.300
I'd say the airplanes are headed for one of those locations.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.760
So we should go somewhere like that too?

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.050
It's way too late for that.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:06.200
Areas with large amounts of American soldiers or where the SDF is stationed

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:08.730
are probably keeping the situation under control.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.000
However, it's likely that they started being strict about who they take in.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:16.330
Actually, before we know it, the whole world will be like that.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.830
What would you do if letting in others meant risking letting <i>them</i> in too?{"those things" to "them(italics)" for clarity -A0}

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.050
I'd shut myself in.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.990
And what if the whole world started thinking the same as you?

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:38.130
What if they tried to keep their community as small as possible for maximum survival?

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.900
Wow Takagi-san, you really are a genius.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.960
What're you acting so surprised about?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.500
Just look at him. He's an example of what I'm talking about.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:52.030
But I doubt that he himself realizes it.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.860
I mean, you know what happened overnight.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.620
Should I stop him?

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:03.430
What we should be doing is thinking about how we're going to survive.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.670
I need someone I can trust...

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.130
Jeez, if only Komuro were here.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.960
Takagi-san, you like Komuro, don't you?

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.030
Don't say something so stupid!

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:22.130
Wh-What?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:26.470
I am concerned about their safety.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.510
It would be preferable if we were able to rejoin them without incident.{"meet them" to "rejoin" -A0}

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:44.430
Shit's awesome! It looks like Hell!

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.270
This is crazy. It's like a war.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.040
This might be worse than a war...

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:56.890
It's too dangerous here.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:57.920
I'm gonna go through it.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:05.460
Hey!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:09.680
Hang on!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:24.070
Why are they trying to kill us? We're still human!

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.720
They're going mad.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.160
Just like we are.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:31.620
Like we are?

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.910
Huh? Isn't the bridge straight ahead?

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.550
Look at the other side of the bridge.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.810
Who knows when we'll be able to cross over.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:55.070
Let's go toward Onbetsu Bridge and try to meet up with the others.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:07.780
I repeat!

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:12.500
Please stay calm and continue to follow police instructions!

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.490
Currently, citywide traffic has been restricted.{"city wide" to "citywide" -A0}

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:23.950
Any unauthorized persons who attempt to cross the river will be reprimanded.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:27.300
Additionally, crossing by foot is also prohibited.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.540
Hey! Wait!

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.510
You were looking at her panties, weren't you?!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.350
Hey, move it!

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.410
Shut up, granny!

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:41.690
Move it!

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.560
Attention, students!

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.050
Do not attempt to cross the bridge!

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.250
This is our final warning!

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:50.130
Don't give me that shit!

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:52.490
As if we'd listen to the cops!

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.120
Who needs them when we've got the juvenile law?!

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.100
You're so cool Hide-chan!{"cool, Hide~" to "cool Hide-chan" -A0}

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.530
Releasing water!

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.540
M-Mr. Officer, they made me...

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:16.330
Releasing water!

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.010
As members of Fujimi Academy,

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:30.970
it's during trying times like these that we must keep our pride!

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.140
We must keep our pride!

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:52.030
Meaning those two who got off the bus, Komuro-kun and Miyamoto-san, don't belong with us anyway!

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.490
Let's stick together in order to survive!

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:56.540
He's seriously insane.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:11:00.590
Let us work together and triumph!

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.260
Indeed.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:02.350
He is comparable to a recruitment officer for a religious cult.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.320
Shidou-sensei!

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.350
Comparable to? No, that's exactly what he's doing.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:08.730
Just look at the people who are listening to his crap.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.840
They're a cult...

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:14.870
This marks the birth of the Shidou Religion.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.470
Look at the situation outside.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.540
In order to escape, I believe we will need to leave this bus.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.360
Somehow, we must make it to the East Police Station by means of crossing Onbetsu Bridge.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.810
I must keep my promise to meet Komuro-kun there.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.230
Wow, you really have Komuro on your mind.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.950
You aren't worried about your family?

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:39.900
I do worry, but the only kin I have is my father. He is overseas at a dojo.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:47.300
As such, all I have to hold onto right now is my life and my promise with Komuro-kun.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:49.750
Father has always taught me

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:54.200
that a promise must be kept,
 even if it should cost you your life.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.610
Where do you all live?

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.930
My house is in the same area as Komuro's on the other side of Onbetsu Bridge.

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:05.550
Uhm, my parents aren't in the neighborhood,

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:09.840
but I'll follow Takagi-san to the end of the world.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:10.850
<i>Gross!{added italics -A0}</i>

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.890
Where is your family, Hirano?

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:18.580
My dad is in Amsterdam buying supplies, since he's a jewel merchant.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:22.600
My mom is a fashion designer and she's been in Paris...

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.040
What the?! What time period is this character sheet from?

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:31.520
If we were in a manga, your dad would be the captain of a foreign cruise ship.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:33.720
Actually, that was my grandpa.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:36.400
My grandma was a violinist.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:39.780
<i>I-It all fits...{Italics added -A0}</i>

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:42.910
So, what are you guys gonna do?

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.290
I wanna come too.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:46.500
You do?

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:51.020
My parents are both dead and my relatives live far away.

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:57.220
It's rude of me to say this,
 but I don't really like Shidou-sensei.

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:00.670
Then what shall we do?

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:02.490
This area is foreign to me.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:05.630
First, we'll check on Onbetsu Bridge.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:08.940
What's wrong, you guys?

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:11.190
We should work together.

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:14.070
Thanks but no thanks, Shidou-sensei.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:17.710
We've got our own agenda.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:21.910
We're not on a field trip, so we have no reason to stay with you.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:24.760
Oh?

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:35.740
If you've decided to leave,
 then feel free to do so, Takagi-san.{added "-san" -A0}

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:40.670
Japan is the land of the free after all.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.440
But...

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.920
It'd be bad if you went, Marikawa-sensei.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:54.110
In this situation, losing our medic would be very problematic.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:55.980
So, how about it?

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:58.150
Won't you stay?

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:03.000
These students are relying on you.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:10.910
Hi-Hirano-kun?

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:13.180
It's not that I missed.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:14.690
I missed on purpose.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.350
S-Since when have you been so viol—

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:21.450
How many corpses do you think I wrecked back at school?

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:23.630
You know,

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:28.480
you've always treated me like crap!

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.950
But I put up with it.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.340
I put up with it for so long!

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.590
I wanted to be normal,

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.350
so I kept putting up with it!

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:45.410
But I don't need to do that anymore.

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:48.220
Normal doesn't mean shit!

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:50.640
That's why...

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:52.710
I can kill.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:56.420
I can kill the living too.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:01.720
H-Hirano-kun, th-that's...{"t-that's..." to "th-that's" -A0}

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:04.830
Busujima-sempai, you should get off first.

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:07.050
I'll guard the rear!

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:12.130
What a fine man you are, Hirano-kun.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.670
Sensei?

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:26.930
It's the same here.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.240
Now what?

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.240
Check on a different bridge?

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.110
That sounds pointless.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:35.040
I bet all of the bridges have been blocked.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.350
Otherwise, there's no reason for the police to be there.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.830
Somehow, we need to get across Onbetsu Bridge

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:47.120
and get to the East Police Station by 7 PM.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:50.020
But how?

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.250
Lemme think!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:54.790
Right now, I wish—

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:55.550
Don't say it!

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.360
Even if you do, things won't change.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:02.720
Gunshots?

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.230
No, that's...

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:13.120
M-M-Maybe it would've been better if we had stayed on the bus with Shidou-sensei!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.340
What's that? I thought you said you hated him?

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:21.820
Well, I really don't like him,
 but I don't like walking either.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.810
Busujima-sempai, I'm low on nails!

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:33.360
Would you like to borrow this?

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:36.310
I'm no good at close range combat!

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:38.500
Right now...

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.970
The only thing I can do is fight!

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:47.820
Wait a sec...

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.540
Takashi?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.180
Nooo!

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.040
Takagi-san!

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:00.250
Damn!

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:07.000
Komuro-kun!

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.250
Double tap!{Isn't this in the Zombie Guidebook, lmao}

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:49.350
Busujima-sempai!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.270
Wow...

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:04.920
It seems we have cleared this area.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:07.920
Wow that was tough!

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:10.280
It's not like you did anything...

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:11.820
Sensei!

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.550
Oh my, Miyamoto-san! What a goincidence!{sic on purpose}

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:18.820
...don't you mean coincidence?

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:20.700
Komuro-kun too!

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:23.740
I take it that Tokonosu Bridge is also closed off.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:26.550
Yup. There's nowhere to go.

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:28.110
In that case,

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:30.130
I am glad to see that you are okay, Komuro-kun.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:32.170
You too, Busujima-sempai.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.000
And what about me?

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.220
Uh yeah nice to see you alive and well too, Takagi.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:39.220
And Hirano!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.330
KOMURO~!

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:42.090
What's this?!

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:43.020
How'd you get it?!

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:44.060
Bullets?

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:48.240
This is the same Smith & Wesson M37 Airweight that the police use, right?!

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.210
W-We can talk about it later...

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:50.740
This one is the Chief's Special...

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:55.620
We exited the bus due to the blocking of the road

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.170
and have been unable to cross the river.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.730
The water level went up.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.130
I guess it wouldn't be possible to go upstream.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.640
So what should we do?

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:07.530
Uhm...

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:10.540
I think we should rest now.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:12.650
"Rest"?

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:17.450
You see, there's a place we can use. It's nearby, so we can walk there.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.060
Is it your boyfriend's?

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:23.640
N-No! It belongs to my female friend!

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:27.130
She's always busy and traveling because of work!

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:30.420
She gave me the key. I go over there while she's gone and let some fresh air in.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.290
Have a nice day~

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.400
Is it an apartment?

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.800
Is the view good?

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:39.990
Yeah!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.500
It's a maisonette that's next to the river.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:44.860
It's close to a convenience store too.

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:52.130
Oh, and she has a car, too.
 It looks like a tank and it's thiiis big!

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:55.050
Well, I'm really tired.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.010
I'd like to shower while there's still working electricity.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.010
S-Sounds good.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:03.100
You perv!

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.890
We'll go check on it first.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:08.270
Get on, Shizuka-sensei.

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:09.450
Okay!

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.960
The breeze is great!

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:23.340
Uhm, Sensei, you don't have to squeeze me...

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.930
Huh? What was that?

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:28.170
I can't hear you~

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:29.600
Uhm, I...

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.640
I can't hear you~

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:32.700
I...

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.090
I can't hear you~

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:37.190
I...

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:47.270
Hadazamui Yozora ni wa Kimi ga Omoiukabu

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:47.270
The chilly night sky makes me think of you

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:47.270
肌寒い夜空には 君が思い浮かぶ

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:54.700
Shizukana Konna Hi ni wa Kimi ni Aitaku Naru

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:54.700
and the quiet day makes me want to see you

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:54.700
静かなこんな日には 君に会いたくなる

00:20:54.700 --> 00:21:03.400
Donna Hi mo Kimi no Koto Mamoritai Kara

00:20:54.700 --> 00:21:03.400
No matter what the day is like, I want to protect you

00:20:54.700 --> 00:21:03.400
どんな日も君の事 守りたいから...

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.400
I want you baby

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:10.880
Hashiridashita Speed de Toozakatteku Hibi

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:10.880
The days that disappear at the same speed they appeared with

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:10.880
走りだしたスピードで 遠ざかってく日々

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:15.710
Tsunaida Te no Nukumori mo

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:15.710
and the warmth we felt in each others hands

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:15.710
繋いだ手の温もりも

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.760
Osanai Koro no Omoidebanashi

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.760
are just vestiges of our childhood

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.760
幼い頃の思い出話

00:21:19.760 --> 00:21:20.770
Time goes by

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:23.890
Kimi wa Mou Wasurete Shimatteirun Darou

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:23.890
I bet you've forgotten those things by now

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:23.890
君はもう忘れてしまっているだろう

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:27.480
Yubikiri Kawashita Yakusoku Sae mo

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:27.480
You probably forgot our promise too

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:27.480
指切交わした約束さえも

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.090
Dakedo Mada Mune no Oku

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.090
I still have it in my heart

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.090
だけどまだ胸の奥

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.090
Nokosareta Kimochi ga

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.090
I won't ever be able to get rid of

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.090
残された気持ちが

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:36.190
Itsumademo Keshisarenai Mama

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:36.190
my remaining feelings for you

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:36.190
いつまでも 消えし去れないまま

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:44.700
Hadazamui Yozora ni wa Kimi ga Omoiukabu

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:44.700
The chilly night sky makes me think of you

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:44.700
肌寒い夜空には 君が思い浮かぶ

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:52.110
Shizukana Konna Hi ni wa Kimi ni Aitaku Naru

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:52.110
and the quiet day makes me want to see you

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:52.110
静かなこんな日には 君に会いたくなる

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:58.750
Kurayami mo Surinukete Tonde Ikeru

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:58.750
I can fly to you while passing through darkness

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:58.750
暗闇もすり抜けて 飛んでいける

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:00.330
I can fly for you

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:09.220
Ano Koro to Kawaranai Boku no Mama de

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:09.220
Just like I did back then

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:09.220
あの頃と変わらない 僕のままで...

00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:08.900
I want you baby

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:21.400
It's a Humvee! And a military model, at that!{"Hum-Vee" to "Humvee" -A0}

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:24.030
See? Doesn't it look like a tank?

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:26.190
What kind of friend do you have?

00:22:26.690 --> 00:22:29.080
I don't think <i>they</i> can climb the fence.

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:31.710
We should be able to sleep peacefully.

00:22:32.390 --> 00:22:33.390
Anyway, we should hurry—

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:41.230
How's this, Komuro?

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:42.960
It's good enough.

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:44.390
Stay back.

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:48.870
Remember to cover for one another.

00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:50.210
Let's go!

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.130
<i>Thinking back on it,</i>

00:22:54.590 --> 00:22:56.210
<i>the way in which we changed was surprising.</i>

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:00.810
<i>At that time, we didn't run away.</i>

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:06.480
<i>In order to survive, we quit running away and started attacking.</i>

00:23:07.590 --> 00:23:11.010
<i>And none of us stopped to question ourselves.</i>

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:13.830
<i>We had changed...</i>

00:23:14.480 --> 00:23:15.680
<i>We had changed so much</i>

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:19.540
<i>in just a day.</i>

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:28.800
Whoa, Sensei... {"Woah" to "Whoa" -A0}

00:23:33.630 --> 00:23:36.440
Keep going and we'll be in trouble.
